<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carlo Lauberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1752">1752</a>–<a href="/years/1834">1834</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carlo Lauberg was a Neapolitan chemist and Jacobin who fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> after a republican conspiracy in 1794. He returned with the French army in January 1799 and became the first president of the provisional government of the Parthenopean Republic. He left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> before the republic's fall and later worked as a pharmacist in the French army.</p></div>
